# Stack

## Languages
- Backend:  <language and runtime, e.g. Rust (Cargo)>
- Frontend: <language and runtime, e.g. TypeScript + React + Vite>

## Commands

### Build
- Backend:  <e.g. cargo build>
- Frontend: <e.g. cd web && npm run build>

### Test
- Backend:  <e.g. cargo test>
- Frontend: <e.g. cd web && npx vitest run>

### Type Check / Lint
- Backend:  <e.g. cargo clippy -- -D warnings>
- Frontend: <e.g. cd web && tsc --noEmit>

### Format
- Backend:  <e.g. cargo fmt>
- Frontend: <e.g. cd web && npx prettier --write src/>

## Quality Tools (install if missing)

Each analyzer below MUST conform to the Analyzer Contract: accepts a path,
emits a single JSON document to stdout (`tool`, `metric`, `threshold`,
`violations`, optional `summary`), exits 0 on pass and non-zero on any
violation.

- Coverage:    <tool name>
  Install:     <install command>
  Run:         <command emitting Analyzer Contract JSON with metric=coverage>
  Threshold:   80  # minimum coverage (%)

- Mutation:    <tool name, e.g. cargo-mutants / mutate4go / Stryker>
  Install:     <install command>
  Run:         <command emitting Analyzer Contract JSON with metric=mutation>
  Threshold:   90  # minimum kill rate (%)

- Complexity:  <tool name, e.g. gocyclo / radon cc / PMD>
  Install:     <install command>
  Run:         <command emitting Analyzer Contract JSON with metric=complexity>
  Threshold:   4   # max cyclomatic complexity per method

- CRAP:        <tool name, e.g. crap4go / custom plugin>
  Install:     <install command>
  Run:         <command emitting Analyzer Contract JSON with metric=crap>
  Threshold:   30  # exclusive upper bound per method

- DRY:         <tool name, e.g. dry4go / jscpd / leave blank to skip>
  Install:     <install command>
  Run:         <command emitting Analyzer Contract JSON with metric=dry>
  Threshold:   <project-specific; omit if DRY not enforced here>

- Lint:        <tool name, e.g. clippy / eslint / ruff>
  Install:     <install command>
  Run:         <command emitting Analyzer Contract JSON with metric=lint>
  Threshold:   0   # zero warnings, zero errors

## Additional Verification
- Tests:       all pass
